==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got,got[UK]:gotten[US]> across}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[cross#Verb|cross]]; to [[move#Verb|move]] from one side (of something) to the other, literally or figuratively.
#: ''In heavy rain, the cavalry couldn't '''get across''' the river.''
#: ''It's impossible to '''get across''' with all checkpoints closed.''
#: ''Bridge the digital divide. Let the poor '''get across'''.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an idea [[evident]]; to successfully [[explain]] a thought or feeling; [[put over]].
#: ''I couldn't '''get across''' to the board this simple economic fact.''
#: ''Better organized writing helps to '''get''' the point '''across'''.''

